  "scope_note": "The old sequential20-call smoke attempt is preserved honestly as owner-interrupted and NOTQUALIFIED: its first14desktop call ended before any PASS cell, with all source guards true and children reaped. The exact owner-interruption receipt, closed result/steps and old log/reaper are saved. No product assertion failure, passed coverage or successful full smoke is inferred from that interruption.\n\nA new frozen grouped runner uses the existing native supported stage list1-3,7-12,14 for desktop thenmobile: exactly TWO real native executions cover TWENTY logical part/viewport pairs, preserving native assertions, waits, timeouts, vendor behavior and page-error checks. Its three frozen payloads and the FIXED actual input BINDING.json are saved. The grouped desktop call is still active and mobile had not started at root1605 closure. CURRENT, live logs, partial reapers, screenshots and runtime results are excluded. Native40453 source/398.969 phone pass/publication remain banked735; full grouped BOTH/current composition/normal merge remain pending.\n\nThe full olderB survivor pack was verified before capacity recovery: header/footer/index and all96,935 OIDs matched, then native Git delta/object validation passed in285.8319 seconds with closed authority guards. The earlier missing-registered-worktree preflight refusal and frozen corrected verifier are retained as separate provenance. Only explicitly approved redundantA pack plus its idx/rev sidecars were removed, physically reclaiming8,756,207,616 bytes. The first pre-unlink refusal and final controller/restore/receipt are preserved. All canonical objects and private/ref/admin/worktree/source authority remain in verified B; only documented byte-identical index-cache normalization was admitted. No pack/index body, further pack retirement or unique-object/source deletion is included or authorized by this archive.\n\nBoth previously retired old lighthouse terrain copies were then restored through native local verified canonical Git blobs, exact bytes/0600/originalmtime/nlink1. The first pre-restore refusal and complete final metadata proof are saved; the note preserves history and clearly states BOTHRESTORED. Neither terrainD hazard remains. The ten modified/untracked lighthouse source authorities remain preserved in732. No sixty-megabyte model copy, whole worktree or private configuration is archived.\n\nSchool, Green Tree and Carpenter were individually renewed natively through18:33-18:34UTC, with all3237 foreign ticket paths/modes exact and only claimed_by/claimed_at changed. OriginalT2378 was legitimately claimed fromOPEN without force under the exact historical ASCII actorbeaubien-lakehouse-agent, valid through19:00:01.941UTC. A first unpublished zero-width-actor typo was blocked before remote push, retained, reset only to its own exact metadata base, then corrected from a frozen ASCII binding. No wrong remote actor, new ticket, group change, source operation or foreign takeover occurred. Complete closed claim proofs are included.\n\nThe closed37dev audit and actual40453-head CI evidence are saved: all four real checks were green/serverclean, while three substantive jobs actually checked synthetic584328 with parents[a248,40453]. The later37 small Kimball geometry reduction/default-producer change is a bounded read-only classification, not a new37 phone/CI result. The grouped ordinary merge controller remains unrun preparation. Current PR body, fresh root1605 recovery and explicit unmerged1456 producer/schema dependencies for parallel School/Beau work are retained. Active isolated clones, private configs and partial native output are excluded until separately closed postimage capsules. No primary/source/app-API/PR/ref change or local tar copy was made by the publisher; every previous evidence path remains intact.",
